{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"Two details matter for the design: restore checks `:image` membership, not equality with the current code-space hash, and calling a captured continuation inside the VM bypasses the external plain-data gate. I’m favoring resumable wasm body functions driven by an explicit trampoline, so guest continuations never depend on the wasm call stack.\n"}}
